# Agency UI — stable preferences

Apply these on every Agency UI / modal / table change unless the user overrides them.

## Copy & language

- Persian UI copy matters: prefer **exact wording** the user provides; do not “improve” marketing tone.
- Prefer short, actionable labels over explanatory chrome (e.g. confirm CTA `درخواست صدور`, not a longer invented phrase).
- Subtitles should explain **what to do**, not dump counts/stats unless asked.
- Align hint/subcopy with the primary button label when the user renames that button.
- Avoid redundant status labels (e.g. don’t show a “already done / travelled” chip if absence is enough).

## Information hierarchy (lists & rows)

- Trip/ticket rows: **passenger full name first**, **route/direction second** (most important).
- Demote codes, national IDs, service names, and dates to secondary meta.
- In confirm cards: passenger + route as the head; do **not** repeat them again in the facts list.
- Sort **actionable/selectable items before blocked/unselectable** ones.
- For cancelled / dead records: **hide action menus** entirely (not just disable items).

## Controls & chrome

- Remove filters/buttons that don’t change a real decision (keep period/search if useful).
- Do **not** add escape hatches (“انتخاب بلیط‌های دیگر”, secondary browse links) on confirm steps unless asked.
- Search fields: include a proper search icon; keep placeholder text readable (no overlap).
- Clear/reset selection: icon button (prefer dismiss/cross), outline-danger idle → **filled danger when there is something to clear**.
- Destructive actions (cancel/delete/revoke): always confirm with a **minimal SweetAlert** before submit; never fire immediately on click.
- After a successful create/issue flow: **navigate to the result** — no celebratory success popup unless asked.
- When an item is blocked/ineligible: honest copy + **hide or disable** the primary submit — never leave a tempting enabled CTA.

## Empty & loading states

- Empty states: compact spacing, vertically tight under toolbar; **no decorative icon** unless the user asks.
- Empty CTAs: one primary action only (e.g. reset filters / go buy); drop secondary “clear search” if redundant.
- Loading states may keep a modest min-height; empty states should not look like a tall hollow box.

## Visual system

- Stay inside the existing Agency stack (Bootstrap + Fluent/Iconify color icons where already used).
- Prefer outline variants for idle secondary actions; filled only for active/affirmative/destructive-ready states.
- Badges: only when they add signal (e.g. “جدید” for very recent). Use a clear red pill for “جدید” when that rule applies.
- Don’t invent purple/glow AI aesthetics; match the current portal look.
- Mobile/tablet drawers & menus: **dim overlay only** — never frost the page with `backdrop-filter` / blur. Keep the drawer above the overlay in z-index.

## Prompt efficiency (when user sends UI polish)

- If several adjacent tweaks target the same surface, implement them as **one pass** and verify once.
- Prefer end-state acceptance (“cancelled rows have no عملیات”) over DOM-path dumps unless location is ambiguous.
- When told to continue: resume the unfinished work directly — no recap, no “I’ll continue”.
